            <persName type="full">John [Chrysostom] Segrue</persName>
            <date type="birth" when="1884-01-07"/>
            <date type="death" when="1942-09-11"/>
            <note type="gender">M</note>
         </ab>
         <div type="bio">
            <p>English journalist, correspondent in Geneva for the <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Daily News</name> during WWI. Following JJ’s altercation with <name type="person" key="ID_MISSING">Henry Carr</name> in 1918 over a dispute involving the English Players, Segrue facilitated the Players’ performance in Geneva through a visit to the British consulate there. Segrue died in a German prison camp after having been captured while covering the war in Yugoslavia for the <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">News Chronicle</name>. <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
